WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.040
Welcome to Data Quality. In this lesson, we explore this purpose: Make data sufficiently accurate, complete and fit for its intended use.

2
00:00:10.040 --> 00:00:20.770
Consider this scenario. A KPI dashboard includes duplicates and obsolete records. First understand the problem before producing documentation.

3
00:00:20.770 --> 00:00:30.650
Start with two steps: Define quality requirements. Then Assess data against criteria. Each step should be explained and evidenced.

4
00:00:30.650 --> 00:00:40.920
Continue with Resolve duplicates and defects. Then Monitor quality and refine controls. Verify the results against the intended outcome.

5
00:00:40.920 --> 00:01:00.380
Stronger evidence looks like this: Stronger: contemporaneous quality rules, validation reports, cleansing log tied to real work. Weaker evidence would be: Weaker: measuring volume rather than suitability of data; no trace of consistent use. Triangulate independent sources.

6
00:01:00.380 --> 00:01:14.630
Now your turn. Review four documents and two interviews, identify inconsistencies and complete the mastery challenge. This video is an independent teaching explanation, not official CMMI model wording.
